  "issue": {
    "body": "HTTP URIs are allowed to have query strings without any values in them, like `/some-url?flag`. I'll call these 'flags'.\r\n\r\nStarlette doesn't appear to provide a way to distinguish between these and not passing the flag at all, so `/some-url?flag` looks identical to `/some-url`.\r\n\r\nI was redirected here after submitting this issue to FastAPI: https://github.com/tiangolo/fastapi/issues/610\r\n\r\nI can work around it by making my clients pass `/some-url?flag=true` instead, so if it's a deliberate design decision not to support this then I understand.",
    "body_last_edited_at": null,
